bc_beacon_info.title=Beacon
bc_beacon_info.line.0=Build a pyramid of iron, gold, emerald, diamond, or netherite blocks under the beacon to power it.
bc_beacon_info.line.1=A bigger pyramid unlocks more effects. Pick one primary effect.
bc_beacon_info.line.2=Pay with one accepted ingot: iron, gold, emerald, diamond, or netherite.
bc_beacon_info.line.3=At pyramid level 4 you can also pick Regeneration as a second effect.
bc_cartography_info.title=Cartography Table
bc_cartography_info.line.0=Copy a map: a filled map and an empty map.
bc_cartography_info.line.1=Zoom out a map: a filled map and paper.
bc_cartography_info.line.2=Lock a map so it cannot change: a filled map and a glass pane.
bc_cartography_info.line.3=Check the recipe in game if a slot does not accept an item.
bc_grindstone_info.title=Grindstone
bc_grindstone_info.line.0=Put two damaged items of the same type in to repair them into one.
bc_grindstone_info.line.1=Remove enchantments from an item. You get experience back for each one removed.
bc_horse_info.title=Horse, Donkey, and Mule
bc_horse_info.line.0=Put a saddle in the saddle slot to ride the animal.
bc_horse_info.line.1=Horses take armor in the armor slot.
bc_horse_info.line.2=Donkeys and mules take a chest to gain extra inventory space.
bc_inventory_info.title=Inventory
bc_inventory_info.line.0=The 2x2 grid crafts items. The result slot shows what you can make.
bc_inventory_info.line.1=The armor slots on the side hold your helmet, chestplate, leggings, and boots.
bc_inventory_info.line.2=The off-hand slot holds a second item, such as a shield or a totem.
bc_loom_info.title=Loom
bc_loom_info.line.0=Put a banner and a dye in the loom to make a new banner design.
bc_loom_info.line.1=A banner pattern in the pattern slot adds a design to the banner.
bc_trade_info.title=Villager Trading
bc_trade_info.line.0=Pick a trade from the list. Each trade shows what you pay and what you get.
bc_trade_info.line.1=A trade runs out after its uses and restocks as the villager's day goes on.
